      "notes": [
         {
            "category": "description",
            "text": "Net::IP::LPM versions before 1.12 for Perl accept malformed prefix lengths.\n\nNon-numeric and non-ASCII prefix lengths are accepted and treated as 0. Integers over 31 bits are silently truncated.  A single malformed mask will poison the lookup table.\n\nThe result is that the lookup will silently succeed for every address. An allow-list will allow every address, and a deny-list will block every address.",
            "title": "Vulnerability Description"
         }
      ],
